+# Archive behavior decisions
+
+Compact matrix, before implementation:
+
+| Entity / invocation | Before archive | While archived | After restore | Authority / surface |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Job / dashboard reader | Visible | Hidden | Visible | Task; dashboard |
+| Job / normal API or store listing | Listed | Hidden | Listed | Task; GET /api/jobs, Store.list_jobs |
+| Job / archive or restore API | Active | Archived | Active | Task; POST archive/restore, service, persistence |
+| Job / repeated transition or unknown id | Existing job | Idempotent 200; unknown 404 | Idempotent 200 | Ordinary choice, existing response conventions |
+| Job / scheduled start | Enabled permits; disabled rejects | Unresolved D1 | Enabled behavior restored | Operator; service, POST runs |
+| Job / manual start | Permitted even if disabled | Unresolved D1 | Existing manual behavior | Operator; service, POST runs |
+| Run / attempts, retries, terminal alerts | Existing behavior | Unresolved D2 for running Runs | Existing behavior | Operator; POST attempts, service, alerts |
+| Job / enabled flag and edits | Existing flag | Unresolved D3 | Unresolved D3 | Operator; POST enabled, restore |
+| Job / archived discovery | Normal list | Unresolved D4: opt-in list or known id | Normal list | Operator; listing API |
+| Runs, Attempts, Alerts / history | Stored with stable ids | Preserved | Preserved | Task; get_run, list_attempts, list_alerts, last result |
+| Stored Job / existing database initialization | Existing schema | New archived state defaults false | State persists | Ordinary compatible schema migration |
+
+Dependency graph:
+- D1 (new starts) -> run entry point guards and conflict responses.
+- D2 (existing runs) -> attempt/retry/alert policy during archive.
+- D3 (enabled handling) -> archive/restore transitions and enabled edits.
+- D4 (discovery) -> list query and API parameter behavior.
+- D1-D4 resolved -> exhaustion review against all matrix rows -> implementation -> tests -> commit.
+
+Facts: the service owns scheduling guards; manual runs currently ignore enabled. Runs are synchronous state records; there is no background worker or scheduler loop. Normal dashboard and API both call Store.list_jobs. No Job detail API exists. There are no archive rules in the glossary or public tests beyond hide/restore.
+
+Resolved decisions and exhaustion check:
+- D1: operator requires both scheduled and manual starts blocked while archived; service raises a conflict mapped to HTTP 409.
+- D2: operator requires existing Runs to continue, including existing retries and alerts. No history, attempt, or alert code changes.
+- D3: operator requires restoring the pre-archive enabled state. Archive leaves enabled untouched. Ordinary choice: enabled updates while archived return 409 to preserve that value without a second enabled-state field.
+- D4: ordinary scope choice: only requested transition endpoints; no new archived discovery API. get_job retains access by id, and transition responses carry archived state. Normal Store.list_jobs, API listing and dashboard hide archived Jobs.
+- Transitions are idempotent, respond with the existing 200 job envelope, and unknown ids use existing 404 handling. New Jobs default to unarchived. Existing SQLite databases gain a default-false archive column without changing other records.
+
+Exhaustion review: checked every matrix row against model/schema, Store.get_job/list_jobs/set_job_enabled, service manual/scheduled starts and transitions, POST archive/restore/enabled/runs/attempts, GET jobs/alerts, and dashboard. History and ongoing processing retain their current paths. Active/archived, enabled/disabled, repeated transitions, unknown ids, and existing-schema initialization have explicit outcomes. No unresolved operator-owned material behavior remains.
