 - [GLOSSARY.md](./GLOSSARY.md)
 - [benchmark scoring](../../docs/benchmarks/SCORING_V0.md)
 - [evaluator protocol](../../docs/benchmarks/EVALUATOR_PROTOCOL_V0.md)
+
+## Archive and restore Jobs
+
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/archive` hides a Job from `/api/jobs` and `/dashboard`.
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/restore` returns it to those views. Both endpoints accept
+an empty body and return HTTP 200 with `{"job": {...}}`, including the boolean
+`archived` field. Repeating either operation is safe; unknown ids return 404.
+Restore uses the known Job id; there is no separate archived listing API.
+
+An archived Job rejects new manual and scheduled Runs with HTTP 409. Existing
+Runs continue through attempts, retries and terminal outcomes with their existing
+alert behavior. Run, Attempt and Alert records are retained. Archive preserves
+the Job's enabled/disabled state; enabled updates return 409 while archived, and
+restore retains that pre-archive state. Jobs created before this feature default
+to unarchived when an existing SQLite connection is opened by Store.
+
+Verify with `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
